/*
  Korean for every string in Sources/MicpegUI/Strings.swift.

  The key is the English text exactly as String(localized:) spells it there, with %@ for a
  String and %lld for an Int. A key that does not match is not an error anywhere: it is never
  found, and the English is shown. scripts/l10n-check.sh compares these keys with the ones the
  compiler extracts, in both directions.

  Register follows README.ko.md: statements end in 합니다, instructions in 하세요. Terms follow
  macOS's own Korean: 시스템 설정, 로그인 항목, 개인정보 보호 및 보안, Finder에서 보기. A device
  name is followed by 을(를), 이(가), 은(는) or (으)로, as macOS writes it, because the last sound of
  the name is not known. Where a sentence needs its arguments in another order they are
  numbered: %1$@, %2$@.
*/

